=Rewrite the SEO title and meta description for this page so it earns more clicks from the searches it already ranks for.

Output language: {{ $('Configure Workflow Settings').first().json.language }}
URL: {{ $('Match WordPress Page IDs').item.json.page_url }}
Current title: {{ $json.current_title || '(none)' }}
Current meta description: {{ $json.current_description || '(none)' }}
H1: {{ $json.h1 || '(none)' }}

Last {{ $('Configure Workflow Settings').first().json.lookback_days }} days: {{ $('Match WordPress Page IDs').item.json.impressions }} impressions, {{ $('Match WordPress Page IDs').item.json.clicks }} clicks, CTR {{ ($('Match WordPress Page IDs').item.json.ctr * 100).toFixed(2) }}% at average position {{ $('Match WordPress Page IDs').item.json.position }} (benchmark for that position: {{ ($('Match WordPress Page IDs').item.json.expected_ctr * 100).toFixed(1) }}%).

Top queries for this page (query | impressions | clicks | position):
{{ ($('Post Top Search Queries').item.json.rows ?? []).map(r => '- ' + r.keys[0] + ' | ' + r.impressions + ' | ' + r.clicks + ' | ' + r.position.toFixed(1)).join('\n') || '(no query data)' }}

Rules:
- Match the search intent of the highest-impression queries and use the main query naturally, ideally near the start of the title.
- Title: at most {{ $('Configure Workflow Settings').first().json.max_title_length }} characters. Meta description: at most {{ $('Configure Workflow Settings').first().json.max_description_length }} characters.
- Give a clear reason to click (specific benefit, number, year, or format) but only claim what the current title, description and H1 support. No clickbait, no invented facts, prices or dates.
- Keep the brand or site name only if the current title has it.
- alt_title must take a different angle from new_title so the two can be A/B tested over time.
- rationale: one sentence in the output language explaining the main change.
